teletype." (brought up earlier on this list)
 
Pavel's exhibit above about representation and implementation of
interesting concepts.
 
"Intellect is fully separable from the emotions, not only in our
minds, but also in our AI implementations."
 
I think all of these exhibits are false, and they all represent an
*attitude* which can produce a variety of assumptions that are
certainly false and may have been necessary to overly optimistic
predictions on the part of many AI scientists.
 
I note in passing that Pavel and I seem to have a lot of opinions in
